{"name":"Holiday Road","hex":"#b1d1e2","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"holiday","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A day on which a religious event or secular celebration is traditionally observed.","A day declared free from work by the state or government."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To take a period of time away from work or study.","To spend a period of time in recreational travel."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/holiday"},{"term":"road","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A way used for travelling between places, originally one wide enough to allow foot passengers and horses to travel, now (US) usually one surfaced with asphalt or concrete and designed to accommodate many vehicles travelling in both directions. In the UK both senses are heard: a country road is the same as a country lane. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Roads in general as a means of travel, especially by motor vehicle."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["At the venue of the opposing team or competitor; on the road.","Of or pertaining to a road bike."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/road"}],"entries":[{"title":"Holiday Road","blocks":[{"text":"\"Holiday Road\" is a 1983 single composed and recorded by American guitarist/singer Lindsey Buckingham. Written for the 1983 film National Lampoon's Vacation, it was also used in the film's sequels National Lampoon's European Vacation (1985), Vegas Vacation (1997) and Vacation (2015). Despite only peaking at number 82 on the Billboard Hot 100 chart during its original release, it has since become one of Buckingham's best known songs."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3e/Holliday_Road_-_Lindsay_Buckingham.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holiday_Road","wikidata":"Q5880473"},{"title":"Holiday","blocks":[{"text":"A holiday is a day or other period of time set aside for festivals or recreation. Public holidays are set by public authorities and vary by state or region. Religious holidays are set by religious organizations for their members and are often also observed as public holidays in religious majority countries. Some religious holidays, such as Christmas, have become secularised by part or all of those who observe them. In addition to secularisation, many holidays have become commercialised due to the growth of industry."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Lathmar_Holi_2022_in_Nandgaon%2C_Uttar_Pradesh_%28edited%29.jpg/330px-Lathmar_Holi_2022_in_Nandgaon%2C_Uttar_Pradesh_%28edited%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holiday","wikidata":"Q1445650"},{"title":"Road","blocks":[{"text":"A road is a thoroughfare from one place to another, primarily used for movement of traffic. Many roads are paved."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Erlangen_Bundesautobahn_73_Auffahrt_Luftbild-20230422-RM-165734.jpg/330px-Erlangen_Bundesautobahn_73_Auffahrt_Luftbild-20230422-RM-165734.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Road","wikidata":"Q34442"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3e/Holliday_Road_-_Lindsay_Buckingham.png/250px-Holliday_Road_-_Lindsay_Buckingham.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3e/Holliday_Road_-_Lindsay_Buckingham.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3e/Holliday_Road_-_Lindsay_Buckingham.png/250px-Holliday_Road_-_Lindsay_Buckingham.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHolliday